  "body": "### ⚠️ Search for existing issues first ⚠️\n\n- [X] I have searched the existing issues, and there is no existing issue for my problem\n\n### Which Operating System are you using?\n\nDocker\n\n### Which version of Auto-GPT are you using?\n\nMaster (branch)\n\n### GPT-3 or GPT-4?\n\nGPT-4\n\n### Steps to reproduce 🕹\n\n* create a plugin, include a file like\r\n```python\r\nfrom typing import Protocol\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Example(Protocol):\r\n    def example_method(self) -> None:\r\n        pass\r\n\r\n\r\nclass NotAPlugin(Example):\r\n    def example_method(self):\r\n        print(\"foo\")\r\n```\n\n### Current behavior 😯\n\nwhen loading plugins the class is recognized as a plugin, a prompt appears:\r\n`WARNING: Plugin NotAPlugin found. But not in the allowlist... Load? (y/n):`\n\n### Expected behavior 🤔\n\nclass is not confused for a plugin\n\n### Your prompt 📝\n\nnot applicable\n\n### Your Logs 📒\n\nWARNING: Plugin AutoGPTExamplePlugin found. But not in the allowlist... Load? (y/n): y\r\nWARNING: Plugin NotAPlugin found. But not in the allowlist... Load? (y/n):",
  "labels": [
    "function: plugins"
  ],
